ented infrastructure fallback. Minimal fix: guard the import and preserve advisory reporting when unavailable.\n\nP2 — .claude/scripts/check-subprocess-tests.py:16\nReconfirmed rc finding: install.sh:1606 copies this checker and its Python helper but omits the required JSON baseline. Default invocation after fresh installation therefore exits 2. Minimal fix: explicitly ship the baseline or exclude this maintenance checker from adopter installations.\n\nP2 — .claude/scripts/check-subprocess-tests.py:21\nReconfirmed rc finding: a nonexistent --root succeeds with zero findings, masking a CI path typo. Confirmed in a read-only invocation. Minimal fix: require an existing directory before scanning.\n\nP2 — .claude/scripts/_subprocess_census.py:187\nNew integration observation: occurrence numbering includes only currently noncompliant calls. Moving a return-code assertion between two identical calls lets the newly unchecked call inherit the old baseline fingerprint; new_findings returns no additions. Confirmed by in-memory AST checks without executing subprocesses. Minimal fix: number identical calls before filtering compliant calls.\n\nFull-tree baseline validation remains limited by redacted and withheld files.","sentence":"The confirmed issues warrant follow-up, but this payload establishes neither a P0 defect nor a false declared condition."}
